---
// The KWG initials for the Intro face of the hero cube — the companion to
// BangkokSkyline on the Where face, same vocabulary: hairline strokes, no
// fill, drawn on when the wall is first seen.
//
// Monoline geometric letterforms, not the faceted mark from the header. The
// mark is a solid shape and would have to be wiped rather than drawn, which
// is a different gesture from the one the skyline established; a monoline
// letter is a stroke, and a stroke can draw itself.
//
// Cap height runs the full 6–46 of the band and the three letters are centred
// across it, because a monogram at this height spans about 160 of 300 units —
// left-aligning it would leave a third of the band visibly empty.
//
// The 300 x 52 viewBox is a measurement, not a taste. The W mark makes the
// Intro label row 72px tall, so the band left over runs 54–100px depending on
// the viewport — a drawing taller than its slot can only shrink into the
// middle of it.
//
// Centred in that band rather than pinned to its top, which is what the
// skyline does: the skyline nearly fills the room it gets, so the two read
// the same, while these initials use half of theirs and pinning them up
// under the label leaves the gap all on one side.
//
// No motion path here: the initials are the animation, so there is no
// [data-mover] and the cube script's dot step simply does not run.
---

<svg
  class="initials"
  viewBox="0 0 300 52"
  fill="none"
  preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  <!-- K — stem, then arm and leg as one path meeting it at mid-height. -->
  <path class="initials__line" data-draw d="M70 6 V46" />
  <path class="initials__line" data-draw d="M106 6 L70 26 L107 46" />

  <!-- W — one unbroken zigzag, the way the brand mark reads. -->
  <path class="initials__line" data-draw d="M118 6 L131 46 L148 18 L165 46 L178 6" />

  <!-- G — a circle opened at the right, closed by the crossbar. -->
  <path class="initials__line" data-draw d="M225.3 13.1 A20 20 0 1 0 225.3 38.9 V26 H213" />
</svg>

<style lang="scss">
  // Fills the positioned box the face gives it and scales to fit, pinned to
  // the top of that box: when the copy needs the room the drawing shrinks
  // rather than shoving the prose off the wall. Absolute rather than a
  // percentage height, which does not resolve against a flex item's box —
  // and sized explicitly, because an SVG is a replaced element whose auto
  // height falls back to its intrinsic one and drops the bottom offset.
  .initials {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    color: var(--c-hairline-bright);
  }

  .initials__line {
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1;
    // The face scales with the viewport; the stroke must not. A hairline is a
    // hairline at every size or it stops being one.
    vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke;
    // Letterforms, so the joins are drawn the way a pen would leave them.
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }
</style>
